From 865838a35def8ded71d19f9432410b88daa42e1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:59:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] engine: HDR10 and SDR outputs for sinks without Dolby Vision

Pass 2 can write the picture itself instead of the tunnel frame, as
XRGB2101010 into the same output buffers. The colour is a 65^3 table,
built on the CPU from the RPU and sampled with the GPU's trilinear
filtering: the RPU's colour metadata decodes the composer's signal
(Profile 5's IPT too) to BT.2020 linear light, written as PQ (HDR10,
the sink maps) or, with each scene's L1 range mapped by BT.2390's EETF
onto SDR's range, as BT.709 gamma 2.4. Per-pixel colour maths (table
or ALU) made pass 2 two to three times as long.

Pass 2 is bound by instruction count, so the display path takes the
chroma of both columns from shared gathers of a 32-bit view of pass 1's
chroma, applies Annex B's taps once to both, keeps it unrounded as the
table's coordinate, and its interior variant skips the letterbox test.

SDR's gain scales all three channels and the desaturation alike and its
transfer is a power, so the decode is kept per entry for the stream and
an L1 change only rebuilds the 1D gain and rescales the entries, in four
slices on their own threads.

On a Pi 5 SDR adds about 4.5 ms a 4K picture to the tunnel's (Profile
5) and 2 ms (Profile 7 FEL); an L1 change takes about 1 ms.

pi_stream_info gains the output kind: the API version is 4. dvbench:
PI_OUTPUT sets the output kind.
